5,1,1,talk,Victoria,,I believe we must ensure any plan is actually staffable. I intend to look into the roster books for the late-turn pool and the crew establishment and maintenance contract to assess our human resource capacity.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Takumi,,I'm not interested in just the current staff. We always repeat the same mistakes because we forget the past. I'll check the two pilots from eight years ago and the completion records of the earlier accessibility programme.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Toshio,,"I agree that the past is instructive, but the present risks are often hidden. I will examine the joint operators' committee minutes and the contingency pricing inside the pre-war shells to identify administrative and physical hurdles.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Daisuke,,Um... I think we should be careful about the long-term costs. I'll look into the balances in the capital ledger and the ticketing contractor fees and paving rates... if that's okay.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Sakura,,I want to know where the time actually goes! I'll check the journey audits on where minutes go and the timed runs and crowd counts mid-city. Let's find the real mysteries!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, your focus on efficiency is valuable, but efficiency means nothing if there is no one available to drive the trains. I hope the others agree that personnel capacity is a primary constraint.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, personnel are just numbers if you don't know why the previous systems failed. If we ignore the history of those pilots, we're just hiring people to manage a disaster we've already had.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, @Takumi, both points are valid. However, we must also consider the external approvals and structural surprises that often derail these projects. Without knowing who holds the veto, staffing and history are secondary.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with everyone. But I'm just worried that if we don't know where the money is coming from, we'll just end up arguing about the budget again later. I hope the ledger helps.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, don't be so worried! Money is important, but imagine the look on people's faces when we fix the parts they didn't even know were slow! That's the best kind of surprise, right?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, I acknowledge the administrative hurdles, but a veto is easier to manage than a total lack of manpower. If the rosters are empty, no amount of approval will make the trains move.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, you're too focused on the now. If the pilots from eight years ago failed because of staffing, we'll see it in the records. Why guess about the future when the answers are already written down?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, records show what happened, but not always why. The ""why"" is often buried in committee minutes or hidden in the physical state of the shells. I prefer to know the actual obstacles before we commit.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I just don't want us to commit to something we can't actually afford in the long run. I'm worried that the headline totals might be misleading if the contractor fees are too high.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Toshio, @Takumi, you're both like detectives! But I bet the real secret is in the journey audits. If we find the hidden time-wasters, maybe we won't need as many people or as much money!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, reducing waste is a noble goal, but it cannot replace a baseline of available staff. I will stick to my investigation of the rosters and contracts to ensure we have a realistic foundation.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, you can keep your baseline. I'll keep the records. If we ignore the closure reports and past failures, we're just walking blindly into a wall we've hit before. I'm not letting that happen.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Toshio,,It seems we have a comprehensive spread of investigations. I will proceed with the committee minutes and contingency pricing. Knowing the hidden costs and the decision-makers will provide the necessary context for your findings.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'll... I'll stick with the capital ledger and the contractor fees then. I just want to make sure we find a way to pay for this without causing more arguments later. I hope it helps.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Sakura,,Yay! Everyone has their mission! I'm going to dive into those audits and counts to find the real bottlenecks. I'll see you all soon with the secrets I find! Let's make this the best plan ever!,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
