34,2,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"My findings are concerning. The late-turn pool is severely depleted, relying heavily on overtime. Furthermore, roadway and signals crews are a third below establishment. We cannot support any plan requiring additional operational intensity.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, that's exactly why we need the records. The late-evening pilot from eight years ago actually hit its cost-recovery targets. If we can replicate that success, maybe we can find a way to fund the staff you're missing.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, @Takumi, we must be cautious. I found that work inside pre-war shells is now plagued by unrecorded voids, causing massive delays. Any plan relying on those structures is a high-risk gamble regardless of staffing.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,Um... I found that the operating subsidy was trimmed again. But there is a ring-fenced construction balance from a lapsed grant. Maybe we can use that? I'm just worried about the ticketing fees... they're way too high.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Guess what! The crowds aren't the real problem! The audits show people spend way more time waiting for connections than in lines. Also, mid-city trips are taking much longer now, even though the platforms aren't any more crowded!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, if mid-city trips are slowing down despite stable crowds, it likely points to the staffing shortages I found. We simply don't have the crew to maintain the pace or the infrastructure.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, don't just blame the staff. The accessibility records show we lost lane-priority stretches to mixed traffic. If the mid-city is slowing down, it's probably because we gave up the road, not because people aren't working.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, @Victoria, both are possible, but consider the administrative side. I found that roadway consents are already delegated to us, making road-based fixes easier. However, any plan involving rail-ferry integration will stall due to data disagreements.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, if road-based fixes are easier, maybe we can use that ring-fenced construction money for them? I'm just... really worried that if we touch the operating budget, we'll just fight about it again.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, that's a great idea! If we use the special money for road fixes, we can speed up those mid-city trips! Let's fix the parts that actually waste time, not just where people complain!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, @Daisuke, road fixes may be easier, but they still require maintenance. With roadway crews a third below establishment, we risk creating new infrastructure that we cannot actually keep operational. We must prioritize stability over expansion.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Sakura"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, stability is just another word for stagnation. We already know from the accessibility records that we lose ground when we don't fight for it. We can't just stop because we're short-staffed; we have to be smarter.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, stability is a luxury we cannot afford if the infrastructure is failing. However, @Takumi, being ""smarter"" means avoiding the pre-war shells. The risk of unrecorded voids makes any deep structural work unpredictable and likely to stall.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think @Toshio is right about the risks. If we avoid the shells and use the ring-fenced construction funds for road-based fixes, maybe we can avoid the budget fights and the structural delays? I just want something sustainable.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, exactly! And @Victoria, if we make the trips faster, maybe the staff won't have to work so much overtime? Let's find a plan that fixes the real time-wasters without digging holes in the ground!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, efficiency does not automatically reduce the need for a baseline of personnel. If we implement a plan that increases frequency or complexity, we will only further exhaust the remaining crews. We must choose a plan that is sustainable.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, sustainability isn't just about current staff; it's about not repeating failures. We know the late-evening pilot worked. If we use the ring-fenced funds for road fixes, we can improve the system without breaking the staff.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, @Victoria, we must align our goals. A plan that avoids the pre-war shells and rail-ferry integration will bypass the most volatile risks. If we focus on road-based improvements, we utilize delegated consents and available funds.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree. If we can find a plan that uses the ring-fenced construction money for road-based fixes, it avoids the operating budget cuts and the risks @Toshio mentioned. I just hope it's enough to be sustainable.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"@Victoria, @Takumi, @Toshio, @Daisuke, we're all agreeing! Let's pick a plan that speeds up the mid-city trips and fixes those connection waits, but stays away from the scary holes in the ground. That's the real secret to success!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Takumi"",""Toshio"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
